    "title": "pandas.DataFrame.pop — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DataFrame.pop#\n\n- \nDataFrame.pop(*item* )[source]#\n- Return item and drop from frame. Raise KeyError if not found. \n  - Parameters\n    - **item** label\n    - Label of column to be popped.\n  - Returns\n    - Series\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame([('falcon', 'bird', 389.0), ... ('parrot', 'bird', 24.0), ... ('lion', 'mammal', 80.5), ... ('monkey', 'mammal', np.nan)], ... columns=('name', 'class', 'max_speed')) >>> df name class max_speed 0 falcon bird 389.0 1 parrot bird 24.0 2 lion mammal 80.5 3 monkey mammal NaN >>> df.pop('class') 0 bird 1 bird 2 mammal 3 mammal Name: class, dtype: object >>> df name max_speed 0 falcon 389.0 1 parrot 24.0 2 lion 80.5 3 monkey NaN",
